  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 245 PM CDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nSurface high pressure returns later Friday night into Saturday \nmorning leading to light winds, clear skies and good radiational \ncooling. Temperatures by Saturday morning will be in the low to mid \n30s with frost conditions likely so make plans now to protect any \nsensitive vegetation! With the surface high and an upper ridge in \nplace, dry conditions are expected for the weekend. Temperatures \nbegin to rebound again by later Saturday into Sunday as southwest \nflow returns. This translates to gradually increasing highs \nthis weekend into early next week with highs in the upper 50s to\nlow 60s Saturday, mid to upper 60s Sunday and then Monday, and \nin the low to mid 70s Tuesday-Wednsday. \n\nThe GFS brings a small system near to through the region on Monday \nbut the going forecast remains dry until mid to later next week when \nthere is a bit more consensus for returning precipitation chances.",
